From 3d4dba0f2f92ae4f5da7a876b045c02d7c5a74f9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Mingyang Sun (Public)" <mingsun@amd.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 08:20:45 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 14/16] fix(clr): gate the scaled fp8/bf8 unpack converts on
 block16 too

The scaled fp8/bf8 -> f16/bf16/f32 converts lower to
__builtin_amdgcn_cvt_scale_pk8_{f16,bf16,f32}_{fp8,bf8}, which require
the same block16-cvt-scale-insts target feature as their fp4 and fp6
counterparts and are therefore unavailable on gfx1250-strict. They were
left under HIP_ENABLE_GFX1250_OCP_BUILTINS, which is 1 there.

Unlike the fp4/fp6 sites these call the builtin unconditionally, with no
__builtin_amdgcn_is_invocable() guard, so the symptom is a hard compile
error rather than a silently zero-filled result: any device code calling
__amd_cvt_fp8*_scale() fails to build for gfx1250-strict with
"'__builtin_amdgcn_cvt_scale_pk8_f16_fp8' needs target feature
block16-cvt-scale-insts".

Move the nine affected functions onto HIP_ENABLE_GFX1250_BLOCK16_BUILTINS
so gfx1250-strict falls through to the software path each of them already
provides:

  __amd_cvt_fp8_to_float_scale      __amd_cvt_fp8x8_to_fp16x8_scale
  __amd_cvt_fp8x2_to_floatx2_scale  __amd_cvt_fp8x8_to_bf16x8_scale
  __amd_cvt_fp8x2_to_fp16x2_scale   __amd_cvt_fp8x8_to_floatx8_scale
  __amd_cvt_fp8x2_to_bf16x2_scale   __amd_cvt_fp8_to_fp16_scale
                                    __amd_cvt_fp8_to_bf16_scale

The affected set was established by compile-testing every one of the 115
__builtin_amdgcn_* the OCP/fp4/fp6/fp8 headers reference, on both targets
(AMD clang 24.0.0git, ROCm/llvm-project 6bd80f15ed27, ROCm 10.2.0). The
gfx1250 -> gfx1250-strict delta is exactly the 15 cvt_scale_* builtins:
3 fp4, 6 fp6/bf6 (already gated) and these 6 fp8/bf8. Each of the 15 was
then compiled with an unconditional call and reports the same required
feature by name. Nothing outside that set differs between the targets.

Verified: gfx1250 device ISA is unchanged (2 block16 instructions, 22
instructions total, byte-identical); gfx1250-strict goes from failing to
compile to 0 block16 instructions and 269 instructions of software
fallback.

Note: whether A0 truly lacks the pk8 forms is still open with the
compiler team -- 9 of the 15 gated builtins are pk8, not pk16. If they
conclude the pk8 converts are available on A0, the fp4 and fp8 gating
here should be reverted and the fix made upstream by splitting
block16-cvt-scale-insts; the fp6/bf6 pk16 gating is correct regardless.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit d1bb7120b73b5731e0a4b9f4e32d4be0919044b4)
---
 .../include/hip/amd_detail/amd_hip_ocp_fp.hpp  | 18 +++++++++---------
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)

diff --git a/projects/clr/hipamd/include/hip/amd_detail/amd_hip_ocp_fp.hpp b/projects/clr/hipamd/include/hip/amd_detail/amd_hip_ocp_fp.hpp
index 5feba8fe..4abd25c5 100644
